# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Every text file here is LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. That has to be *stated*, because Git for Windows — which GitHub's
# windows-latest runner installs with its installer defaults, and which most
# Windows contributors have on their machines too — sets core.autocrlf=true.
# A plain checkout on Windows then rewrites every .go file to CRLF, and gofmt
# counts CRLF as unformatted: the lint step in the Windows CI job reported
# "File is not properly formatted" for every file in the terminal adapter, each
# pointing at line 1. Nothing was wrong with the code; the line endings of the
# checkout were the whole finding.
#
# text=auto  normalize on commit (LF in the index), and leave anything that
#            looks binary alone.
# eol=lf     check out with LF. Attributes win over core.autocrlf, which is
#            what makes this the fix rather than a workaround — and it fixes
#            the contributor's machine in the same stroke, so `make lint` there
#            stops inventing diffs it cannot explain.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The binary files, named instead of inferred. Content detection is usually
# right, but a fixture that happens to read as text must never be "normalized":
# adapter-guide/tlv-samples/*.bin are byte-exact TLV recordings that the
# adapter tests replay.
*.bin  binary
*.gif  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.wav  binary
*.webp binary
